---
import SwissLayout from '../../layouts/SwissLayout.astro';
---

<SwissLayout title="Track Record — persio.fyi" description="Infrastructure and systems engineer. Twenty-five years of networks, incidents and automation; now building AI-first systems with deterministic verification.">

  <div class="space-y-12 max-w-4xl">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-b border-black pb-4">
        <div>
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black tracking-tighter uppercase">
            Persio
          </h1>
          <p class="font-mono-swiss text-xs text-neutral-700 uppercase mt-1 font-semibold">
            Infrastructure &amp; Systems Engineer &middot; AI-First Systems
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="font-mono-swiss text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
        This page is a sketch, not a résumé. It says what I work on and how; it does not list employers, clients or credential numbers. Ask if you need the formal document.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 00 // IN SHORT -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight uppercase mb-2">
          00 // In Short
        </h2>
        <div class="rule-heavy mb-4"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed font-sans">
        Twenty-five years keeping large networks up: carrier backbones, financial-market connectivity, data-center fabrics and, lately, cloud-delivered security. Most of that time was spent as the engineer of last resort for accounts that cannot afford downtime. Today I apply the same discipline to systems built around language models: small deterministic gates, evidence before claims, and humans who ratify rather than retype.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 01 // DOMAINS -->
    <section class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight uppercase mb-2">
          01 // Domains
        </h2>
        <div class="rule-heavy mb-6"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs font-mono-swiss">
        <div class="border border-black p-4 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-black text-sm uppercase text-black">Routing &amp; Fabric</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">Provider-grade IP routing, MPLS services, multicast, data-center switching fabrics. Greenfield and brownfield.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-black p-4 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-black text-sm uppercase text-black">Security Edge</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">Cloud-delivered security, zero-trust access, next-generation firewalls and the operational reality of running them at scale.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-black p-4 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-black text-sm uppercase text-black">Incidents &amp; Escalation</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">Major-incident ownership, root-cause analysis, change risk, and the writing that makes an outage teachable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-black p-4 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-black text-sm uppercase text-black">AI-First Systems</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">Multi-agent coordination, typed decision gates, local models where they suffice, shell and Python automation with verifiable outputs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 // ERAS -->
    <section class="space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight uppercase mb-2">
          02 // Eras
        </h2>
        <div class="rule-heavy mb-6"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <article class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-6 pb-8 border-b border-black/20">
          <div class="md:col-span-3 font-mono-swiss text-xs font-bold text-neutral-600 uppercase">2024 — Present</div>
          <div class="md:col-span-9 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-black uppercase">Cloud security, customer side</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">Helping enterprises adopt and operate a SASE platform: architecture health, migration sequencing, knowledge transfer. In parallel, building my own AI-first tooling and this laboratory.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-6 pb-8 border-b border-black/20">
          <div class="md:col-span-3 font-mono-swiss text-xs font-bold text-neutral-600 uppercase">2012 — 2024</div>
          <div class="md:col-span-9 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-black uppercase">High-touch engineering at a network vendor</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">A decade as dedicated engineer, then technical lead, for a handful of zero-downtime accounts in banking, exchanges and telecom. Escalations, readiness reviews, software strategy, high-risk changes.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-6 pb-8 border-b border-black/20">
          <div class="md:col-span-3 font-mono-swiss text-xs font-bold text-neutral-600 uppercase">2006 — 2012</div>
          <div class="md:col-span-9 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-black uppercase">Operations and engineering management</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">Led operations and engineering teams at service providers: IP backbones, access networks, financial-market data connectivity, budgets and vendors.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-6 pb-4">
          <div class="md:col-span-3 font-mono-swiss text-xs font-bold text-neutral-600 uppercase">1998 — 2006</div>
          <div class="md:col-span-9 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-black uppercase">Foundations</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">Support, administration, provisioning and project roles across ISPs, hosting and carriers, plus a stretch teaching networking.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 // CREDENTIALS -->
    <section class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight uppercase mb-2">
          03 // Credentials
        </h2>
        <div class="rule-heavy mb-6"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-black p-4 space-y-2 font-mono-swiss text-xs">
        <p class="text-neutral-800 leading-relaxed">Expert-level vendor certification in enterprise infrastructure, active. Business degree. Native Portuguese, fluent English, working Spanish.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

</SwissLayout>
